<BaseLayout title="About Seller Operations Lab" description="Why Seller Operations Lab exists, what it covers and how its guides and experiments are produced." activeNav="/about/">
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell"><p class="eyebrow">SELLER OPERATIONS LAB</p><h1>About the project</h1><p>Independent research and small browser tools for practical Etsy listing workflows.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <h2>A deliberately small scope</h2>
    <p>Seller Operations Lab is not an Etsy integration, image retouching suite or marketplace management service. It does not upload your photos or promise marketplace acceptance. The tools create local exports and the editorial pages state their sources and limitations.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible for the information</h2>
    <p>Seller Operations Lab is the project and editorial identity responsible for this site's guides, references and tools. It is not a claimed team of professional photographers or Etsy sellers. Technical guides and software may be developed with AI assistance; claims about platform behavior are linked to official documentation, while independent workflow advice and reproducible tests are labeled separately.</p>
    <p>The project currently uses <strong>damaheritage.com</strong> as its technical home; Seller Operations Lab is the current editorial identity on that domain. The domain and project are independent of Etsy, Shopify and Google.</p>
    <h2>Useful explanations, not invented credentials</h2>
    <p>Examples are calculations, checklists and browser tests. We do not invent testimonials, sales results, user counts or personal experience. Platform references link to their original documentation; our presets are independent starting points.</p>
    <h2>Funding and independence</h2>
    <p>The tools are free to use. The site may seek advertising support, but the current version does not load advertising or analytics scripts. Each marketplace reference displays the date its official source was last checked. If a source-backed claim is found to be wrong, the project will correct the text and its review date; no response-time promise is made. The public <a href="/contact/">correction tracker</a> is the contact channel; there is currently no private support inbox.</p>
    <p><a href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a> or <a href="/contact/">report a correction</a>.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
